From: Noahcdls <noahcdls@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm8550-lpass-lpi: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The LPI pin controller only has runtime PM ops and holds the ADSP votes
LPASS_HW_MACRO and LPASS_HW_DCODEC as PM clocks. It is a supplier of the
SoundWire controllers, so when one of them is still runtime-active at
system suspend the pin controller keeps both votes for the whole sleep and
the SoC does not reach CX collapse or AOSS sleep. Force the runtime
suspend across system sleep, like the macros and the SoundWire controller.

SM8550 copy of Armada 0565 (armada-os/armada 98e87a101559, SM8650 only
there), the same line as kernel-tb321fu 0021. Qualcomm posted the SM8650
version to linux-arm-msm on 2026-11-12
(20261112-lpass-lpi-system-sleep-v1-1-438cb997e0e9@oss.qualcomm.com).
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
index 875e04e..4c565b9 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -213,6 +213,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pinctrl_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
